# Host / guest model

- There is exactly **one host**. It runs the desktop agent and owns the displays being captured.
- **Guests** are only web browsers on other machines (real hardware or VMs, any OS). They render the host stream via the frontend. Nothing is installed on guests.
- A real macOS machine on the same LAN opening the webapp is a **viewer**, not an agent host.
- Viewer browser in current setup: Brave (Chromium) on macOS — prefer Chromium WebRTC behavior over Safari-only assumptions.
- "macOS guest" means a browser on that Mac viewing the host — not an agent running there.
- Screen capture, PipeWire/SCK portals, and agent logs always refer to the **host**.
- Do not suggest installing or running the agent on a viewer machine unless the user explicitly changes this model.
